We already know what a Traditional/ commercial bank deposit is.
A tokenized deposit is an commercial bank deposit recorded as a digital token on a blockchain. This blockchain is a programmable platform or shared ledger. 
Tokenized deposit remains a direct claim on the issuing bank or financial institution. Its a issuing bank/ FI's liability.
Basically Tokenized deposits belong to Traditional Finance (aka TradFi), however they also do act as a bridge into Decentralized Finance (aka DeFi). 
In other words, Tokenized deposits are digital representations of traditional bank deposits issued on a blockchain by regulated financial institutions, and since they are regulated, Tokenized deposits retain the exact same regulatory and legal protections as traditional bank deposits.
Since tokenized deposits exist on-chain (using distributed ledger technology), they are also used frequently in institutional DeFi to integrate traditional banking money with programmable smart contracts
